id: ops-5mv7
title: Escaped shell metacharacter in scalar value bypasses the attestation gate
description: ""
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-29T03:51:05.208Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-29T03:51:29.200Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-29T03:51:28.995Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-29T03:51:28.995Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T03:51:22.137Z",pi-agent,"CodeRabbit found that FLAG=--provenance\\; unescapes to --provenance; inside shellScalars. The semicolon was not in the rejection character class, so the value was stored. When expanded into a publish command, tokenizeCommands splits on the semicolon, so the scan sees --provenance as a flag while the shell passes --provenance; as a literal argument. Fixed by extending the character class to also reject ;, &, |, <, >, {, } after unescaping. Added end-to-end regression test."
close_reason: "Fixed: extended shellScalars rejection character class to include ;, &, |, <, >, {, }"
body: ""
